    {
      "id": "claim_c7ad7d21b58643d6b0d27bad6b4bb55e",
      "statement": "Failure semantics: a failed summary logs a warning and runs the turn uncompacted (compaction triggers below the limit, so the turn's own prompt still fits), while cancellation always propagates and an explicit /compact rethrows; the UI sees compacting/compacted stream events around the attempt.",
