    {
      "id": "claim_eb4463778eb5492d873b44f5b885766d",
      "statement": "A CompactionCheckpoint is stored keyed chatId.compactedTo (so a chat's checkpoints sort by boundary and history paging can find the one before a cut) and carries the summary (injected into replay as a user message in sanitized <prior_conversation> tags), the chatBindings name map as of the boundary (seed layer + capsules + successful createGadget calls + accepted connection requests + changes-message createdGadgets + PARAMS_<n> callback names), the nextChangeId counter, the chat's pins and epoch, and the composed proposedChange of every still-proposed batch below the boundary.",
