    {
      "id": "claim_2a30ea14c63e4f54b2621f688b14765b",
      "statement": "The checkpoint's pins/epoch are folded from the previous checkpoint over the compacted span (an epoch-boundary merge or migration conversion boundary resets both), and its proposedChange is the composition of all still-proposed batches folded by foldProposedChanges — bounded by content size rather than edit count; the same fold seeds the UI's proposed-changes view via getProposedChanges, which scans the registry when the compacted prefix created gadgets or bindings with no change content.",
