    {
      "id": "claim_6b3640ae55e6440ca9cb948615efaeb8",
      "statement": "Committing a checkpoint stores it and points the chat at it in one synchronous transaction that also deletes meta.totalTokens (so the shrunken prompt is re-measured and can re-trigger); a revert across the boundary calls rollbackChatCompaction, which repoints the chat at the newest checkpoint the revert leaves intact and deletes checkpoints that folded in the erased changes — which is what lets a revert cross a boundary at all.",
